[4537]="700304A5\n1\tDefeat Easterling Horsemen (total: 3)\tMounted Easterlings train on their newly acquired horses outside their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr. You should defeat the Easterling Horsemen, for they are powerful and dangerous foes.\n2\tReturn to Guthferth, Sergeant of North-torr\tSergeant Guthferth rallies the defences of North-torr just north of Floodwend, attempting to hold back the flood of Easterlings threatening to drown the Wold in chaos. You should speak with Sergeant Guthferth.\n",
[4538]="7002EEF3\n1\tDefeat Easterlings at the South Undeep\tEasterlings can be found at the South Undeep. You should defeat many Easterlings in the northern Wold.\n2\tDefeat Easterlings at the South Undeep (total: 12)\tEasterlings can be found at the South Undeep. You should defeat many Easterlings in the northern Wold.\n3\tTalk to Adbert at the northern tower\tAdbert is at the northern watch-tower at the river's edge in the northern Wold. You should talk to Adbert at the northern watch-tower.\n",
[4539]="7004D071\n1\tTravel to Dale\tThe city of Dale can be found north of Lake-town in the Dale-lands. You should travel to Dale.\n2\tFind King Bard II\tYou should find King Bard II, who can be found in the Great-keep in the north part of Dale.\n3\tComplete the Refugees in Dale quest arc\tYou should continue assisting King Bard II in Dale. The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing the Refugees in Dale quest arc which begins with King Bard II in Dale.\n4\tTalk to Queen Regent Erna\tYou should talk to Erna, who can be found in the Great-keep in Dale.\n5\tThe Easterling refugees can be found throughout Dale. You should speak with the Dorwinion and Chayasír Easterlings who have come within Dale's walls.\t\n6\tYou should reassure the concerned Dale-folk that they are not in danger from the Easterling refugees.\t\n7\tDistressed Dorwinions can be found in Dale. You should comfort Dorwinions, still in shock from the devastation in the east and the difficulties of acceptance from some of those in the city of Dale.\t\n8\tReturn to Erna\tYou should talk to Queen Regent Erna, who can be found within the Great-keep in Dale.\n",
[4540]="700266E5\n1\tScout the eastern gate to Annúminas\tThe eastern gate of Annúminas is to the south of the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nimbellas asked you to scout the eastern gate of Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp within the Way of Kings. Nimbellas will be dismayed to hear about the strength of Angmar's encampment at the eastern gate of Annúminas.\n",
[4541]="70043A00\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Eastern Gondor tokens allowance.\n",
[4542]="7002EFB1\n1\tDefeat mounted Easterlings in the eastern plains of the Wold (total: 10)\tMounted Easterlings can be found in the eastern plains of the Wold. Wigbald asked you to defeat the Easterlings rampaging through the farms of the Wold.\n2\tTalk to Wigbald\tWigbald is at Harwick. Wigbald will be pleased to hear that many mounted Easterlings were defeated.\n",
[4543]="70008856\n1\tReturn to Taskmaster Ghamp at the Grimwood Lumber-yard\030Collect Grimwood-kindling (total: 10)\tGrimwood-kindling can be found throughout the Grimwood area, from fallen timber. You might also find it on the Leafcull-trees in the wood. Taskmaster Ghamp, in his own way, directed you to get Grimwood-kindling for repairs at the lumber-yard.\n",
[4544]="7003A590\n1\tDefeat Harrowing Wargs (total: 8)\tHarrowing Wargs can be found throughout the Harrowdale. You have encountered a vicious Warg while exploring the Harrowdale. You should defeat more of its kind to protect the people of Underharrow.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Wargs lurking too near to Underharrow and protected the defenceless people of Kingstead.\n",
